course: dictionary
lesson: 14590
title: Plodding: slow and steady
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Plodding describes something moving or working slowly. Think of heavy boots going step, step, step up a hill. «The tired farmer was plodding home after a long day.» The clues are tired and long day, so plodding means walking slowly and heavily.
explain: Plodding can also describe work. «Mia's plodding work on her model took all week, but she never gave up.» Here plodding means slow and steady, with no rush and not much excitement. Steady work is a good thing, so plodding is not always bad.
explain: Plodding can describe a story or film too. «The film was so plodding that I checked my watch twice.» If you keep checking your watch, the film must be slow and dull. Always ask: does this sentence sound kind or unkind? The context will tell you.
fact: Plodding means walking slowly and heavily, or working slowly and steadily.
fact: Plodding is the -ing form of the verb plod: plod, plods, plodded, plodding.
fact: A plodding worker can be steady and reliable, like the tortoise in the famous race.
fact: «A plodding film» means a film that is slow and dull, with no exciting parts.
fact: Calling a person plodding can be unkind if you mean they are dull, so think about the context first.
exercise: «The plodding horse pulled the cart up the hill.» What does plodding show about the horse? | It is asleep in a field | *It is walking slowly and heavily | It is flying fast over the hill | It is singing a happy song
exercise: «The plodding film had no exciting parts.» What does plodding mean here? | Short and sweet | Fast and funny | *Slow and dull | Loud and bright
exercise: «Dad is a steady, reliable worker who never rushes.» Which word best fits the gap? Dad is a ___ worker. | *Plodding | Flying | Sparkling | Noisy
test: «The tortoise was plodding along the path, one slow step at a time.» What is the tortoise doing? | *Walking slowly | Moving quickly | Sleeping | Jumping
test: Nadia says plodding means exciting. Is she right? | Yes, it means fast and thrilling | Yes, it means bright and cheerful | *No, plodding means slow and steady, not exciting | Yes, it means loud and noisy
exam: Which sentence uses plodding to mean slow and steady work? | The plodding rocket zoomed past the moon in a second | The plodding fireworks lit up the sky with bright colours | *Sam's plodding practice on the piano helped him improve each week | The plodding bell rang out loudly across the field
